<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Placeholder Image in Rails</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Using Placeholder Image with Rails</h1>

    <p>
      This is a simple demonstration of using the placeholder-image middleware
      within a <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/">Rails</a> application.
    </p>
    <p>
      The middleware is mounted at <code>/img/ph/</code>, rather than
      the default <code>/placeholder</code> prefix.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <p>Here is a 120 × 120 pixel image using the default colors:</p>
    <img
      src="/img/ph/120.png"
      width="120"
      height="120"
      alt="Generated 120x120 placeholder image"
    >
    <p>
      <a href="/img/ph/120.png" target="_blank">Open the image directly.</a>
    </p>

    <hr>

    <p>Here is a 300 × 180 pixel image using custom colors:</p>
    <img
      src="/img/ph/300x180.png?bg=111&fg=f90"
      width="300"
      height="180"
      alt="Generated 300x180 placeholder image"
    >
    <p>
      <a href="/img/ph/300x180.png?bg=111&fg=f90" target="_blank">Open the image directly.</a>
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
